.th RTI II 8/12/77
.sh NAME
rti - return from signal trap
.sh SYNOPSIS
rti(ps, pc, sp);
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it rti
executes a
.it signal
0, causing the PSW status, program counter and stack pointer
to be given the values of the three arguments.
The PSW status is first verified to prevent user processes from getting
into an "unauthorized" state.

See signal(II) for details.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
signal(II)
